title: |md
  # Sync — anti-entropy, then live gossip
  On every connection and at app start, two peers reconcile the gap. Live gossip keeps them in step afterwards; it is lossy and unordered, so it is never the correctness guarantee.
| {near: top-center}

shape: sequence_diagram

phone: Phone
tablet: Tablet

phone -> tablet: "connect — QUIC (mDNS · hole punch · relay)"
phone -> tablet: "heads() — the newest HLC I have per device"
tablet -> phone: "heads()"
phone -> tablet: "missing(your heads) — only the gap"
tablet -> phone: "missing(your heads) — only the gap"
phone -> phone: "verify every signature, then insert (set union)"
tablet -> tablet: "verify every signature, then insert (set union)"
phone -> tablet: "live gossip: new events, per baby topic"
phone -> phone: "fold the log into the SQLite projection"
tablet -> tablet: "fold the log into the SQLite projection"
